// Audit C2: writing a `for` counter from inside a nested statement. The old
// check scanned only the body's TOP-LEVEL statements for `i = ..` / `i += ..`,
// so one level of nesting slipped past it — and the backends then DISAGREED:
// the interpreter re-seeded the counter each iteration and printed 99/99/99,
// while the JIT let the write stick and printed 99 once. A live PARITY_FAIL
// with no fixture. Now rejected at analysis time by both.
for i in 0..3 {
    if i >= 0 { i = 99 }
    print(i)
}
